      'Think of retrieval as finding the relevant pages before writing an answer.',
      '1. Ingest approved runbooks; chunk and index with source IDs.\n2. Authenticate the user and restrict retrieval to allowed data.\n3. Retrieve relevant passages; optionally rerank them.\n4. Ask for an answer supported by the supplied passages.\n5. Return source links; abstain when support is insufficient.\n6. Evaluate retrieval quality and answer grounding separately.',
